{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.binghamton.edu/offices/human-resources/jobs/": {
      "title": "Jobs",
      "description": "Jobs | Human Resources | Binghamton University Skip to main content Binghamton University: The State University of New York Human Resources search menu Search Human Resources Human Resources Jobs Faculty, Librarian and Professional Classified Employment Other Employment Job Fair Prospective Employees Employees Benefits Payroll Retirees Contact Jobs Employment Opportunities Thank you for considering Binghamton University in your career search. The premier\n               public university in the northeast is not only a great place to learn — it's a great\n               place to work! Binghamton has earned a reputation as the premier public university in the Northeast\n               because of its exceptional, innovative academic programs, outstanding students, faculty\n               and staff, and the graduation rates. For 60 years, we have been sustained by a vision\n               of excellence that has earned us accolades as the \"crown jewel\" of New York State's\n               public university system. Take a moment to hear what some of our faculty and staff have to say about working at one of \"America's Best Employers by State\" according to Forbes. Read more about us or visit our YouTube site . Applicant Information There are several employers on the Binghamton University campus. For state employee\n               positions, recruitment is decentralized to hiring departments. Depending upon the\n               type of vacancy, the application process will vary. For specific information, choose\n               the vacancy and/or employer from the list below. Binghamton University and the State University of New York are Equal Opportunity/Affirmative\n               Action Employers. Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer The State University of New York is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer.\n               As required by title IX and its implementing regulations Binghamton University does\n               not discriminate on the basis of sex in the educational programs and activities which\n               it operates. This requirement extends to employment and admission. Inquiries about\n               sex discrimination may be directed to the University Title IX Coordinator or directly\n               to the Office of Civil Rights (OCR). Contact information for the Title IX Coordinator\n               and OCR, as well as the University's complete Non-Discrimination Notice may be found here. It is the policy of Binghamton University to provide for and promote equal opportunity\n               employment, compensation, and other terms and conditions of employment without discrimination\n               on the basis of sex, age, race, color, religion, disability, national origin, gender\n               identity or expression, sexual orientation, veteran or military service member status,\n               marital status, domestic violence victim status, genetic predisposition or carrier\n               status, or arrest and/or criminal conviction record unless based upon a bona fide\n               occupational qualification or other exception. For more information visit the Office of Diversity, Equity and Inclusion website at Office of Diversity, Equity and Inclusion Current Vacancies Faculty, Librarian & Professional Complete list of Faculty & Staff vacancies List of Faculty and Librarian vacancies which you apply for \"online\" About professional vacancies — Questions related to online applications Classified Service Civil Service vacancies including nursing, police, trades, clerical, custodial and\n                  others Research Foundation The Research Foundation for SUNY at Binghamton provides essential administrative services\n               that enable SUNY faculty to focus their efforts on the education of students and the\n               performance of life-changing research.  As a private not-for-profit corporation, we\n               support over $50 million in SUNY Binghamton research activity annually, providing\n               sponsored programs administration as well as general administrative support services\n               to SUNY faculty performing research in numerous disciplines. Complete list of Research Foundation vacancies Student Employment All student employment listings are available online through the hireBING system which\n               is maintained by the Fleishman Center for Career and Professional Development and the Financial Aid Services office. Please Search hireBING for Available Positions. Other Employment Opportunities and Related Information Dual Career Program (DCP) View employment opportunities on campus , at State University campuses, other New York state agencies and non-state employers. Clery Act Notification, Drug and Alcohol Free Workplace, Policy on Domestic Violence\n                     in the Workplace, and Training Reminder Human Resources Jobs Faculty, Librarian and Professional Classified Employment Other Employment Job Fair Prospective Employees Employees Benefits Payroll Retirees Contact Return to Top © 2026 Binghamton University State University of New York Accessibility Emergencies Privacy contact visit share Last Updated: 9/16/25"
    },
    "https://www.binghamton.edu/offices/human-resources/jobs/professional.html": {
      "title": "Faculty, Librarian and Professional",
      "description": "Faculty, Librarian and Professional | Human Resources | Binghamton University Skip to main content Binghamton University: The State University of New York Human Resources search menu Search Human Resources Human Resources Jobs Faculty, Librarian and Professional Classified Employment Other Employment Job Fair Prospective Employees Employees Benefits Payroll Retirees Contact Faculty, Librarian and Professional Thank you for considering Binghamton University in your career search. Applications for all professional vacancies are accepted online through our applicant\n               tracking system. Due to Affirmative Action guidelines, applicants must apply to specific vacancies\n               at the University.  Hiring for all professional vacancies is decentralized to the\n               departments on campus and new search committees are formed for each vacancy. Binghamton University and the State University of New York are Equal Opportunity/Affirmative\n               Action Employers Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer It is the policy of the Binghamton University to provide for and promote equal opportunity\n               employment, compensation, and other terms and conditions of employment without discrimination\n               on the basis of age, race, color, religion, disability, national origin, gender identity\n               or expression, sexual orientation, veteran or military service member status, marital\n               status, domestic violence victim status, genetic predisposition or carrier status,\n               or arrest and/or criminal conviction record unless based upon a bona fide occupational\n               qualification or other exception. Faculty, Librarian & Professional Vacancies Complete list of Faculty & Staff vacancies — main listing of professional vacancies Internal Applicant Information Am I an Internal Applicant? Under the Binghamton University UUP Internal Promotion Procedure there are two groups\n               of employees considered as internal applicants: Tier 1 internal applicant: a UUP professional employee with at least one (1) year of service on the basis of\n                  a Term, Permanent or Temporary appointment. In the case of a temporary appointment,\n                  it includes only those who have come to their position as a result of an approved\n                  Affirmative Action search process. Tier 1 internal applicants are given first review\n                  and consideration. Tier 2 internal applicant: University employees represented by classified service bargaining units, designated\n                  management confidential or Research Foundation employees with at least one (1) year\n                  of service. All others are considered external applicants. Interview Exchange — Applicant Tracking System Returning Applicants may sign in here Frequently Asked Questions about Applying Online Binghamton University is a tobacco-free campus. Human Resources Jobs Faculty, Librarian and Professional Classified Employment Other Employment Job Fair Prospective Employees Employees Benefits Payroll Retirees Contact Return to Top © 2026 Binghamton University State University of New York Accessibility Emergencies Privacy contact visit share Last Updated: 9/16/25"
    },
    "https://www.binghamton.edu/offices/human-resources/jobs/classified.html": {
      "title": "Classified Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Classified Employment Opportunities | Human Resources | Binghamton University Skip to main content Binghamton University: The State University of New York Human Resources search menu Search Human Resources Human Resources Jobs Faculty, Librarian and Professional Classified Employment Other Employment Job Fair Prospective Employees Employees Benefits Payroll Retirees Contact Classified Employment Opportunities Classified Service Employment Opportunities Classified Service positions available at the university are within the purview of\n               NYS Civil Service.  Some positions are within the competitive class service and some\n               are non-competitive or labor class. Competitive and non-competitive vacancies are posted as contractually required for\n               the required number of days and, in general, university employees are considered first\n               for vacancies. If the university is unable to identify a qualified, internal candidate for a given\n               position, we then accept applications from external applicants. Classified Service Employment Application Accepting Applications for Custodial Positions. Click here to apply! ** If you need assistance filling out an online application, please visit Broome-Tioga\n                  Workforce NY in the Oakdale Commons at 501 Reynolds Rd, Johnson City, NY 13790. For\n                  more information, go to https://broometiogaworks.com/ Plant Utilities Assistant And Plant Utilities Engineer 1 Continuous Recruitment Human Resources will be accepting applications for the Plant Utilities Assistant and\n               Plant Utilities Engineer 1 positions on a continuous recruitment basis. Please review the Exam Announcement and the minimum qualifications for the PUA and\n               PUE 1 on the Civil Service website by Clicking Here . Individuals interested applying to either the Plant Utilities Assistant and Plant\n               Utilities Engineer 1 positions should submit a NYS-APP #20-450 & #20-451 and a Binghamton\n               University employment application to Human Resources. https://www.cs.ny.gov/extdocs/pdf/20-450&20-451.pdf Competitive The competitive class includes all positions for which it is practical to determine\n               the merit and fitness of applicants by competitive (civil service) examination.  Most\n               clerical positions fall within this class as do most support staff positions.  Only\n               those eligible for transfer, reinstatement or reachable on the appropriate civil service\n               list may be considered to fill competitive class civil service vacancies. This table contains a list of Competitive Classified Service Vacancies Grade Title Department Starting Salary Status Posting End Date SG-6 Office Assistant 1 (Stores/Mail) (NY HELPS) - NO EXAM REQUIRED* Facilities Management $37,862.00 Contingent Permanent, Full-Time 09/05/2026 SG-6 Office Assistant 1 (Stores/Mail)* Facilities Management $37,862.00 Contingent Permanent, Full-Time 09/05/2026 *Interested candidates should submit a NYS Examination /Application (NYS-/APP) to the Office of Human Resources in person or by email to canvass@binghamton.edu . **Interested candidates for the Plant Utilities Engineer 1 or Plant Utilities Assistant\n               positions should submit a NYS-APP #20-450 and a Binghamton University employment application to the Office of Human Resources\n               in person or by email to megwan@binghamton.edu. ***To be eligible to apply to the traineeship, candidates must have one year of permanent\n               service as a Grade 6 Office Assistant and are required to pass a typing test. If you\n               have previous eligible service in a keyboarding title, the typing test is waived.\n               If you are currently an SG-11 Administrative Assistant 1, you may apply for a lateral\n               transfer. NY HELPS : Above titles with NY HELPS included in the name are part of the New York Hiring\n               for Emergency Limited Placement Statewide Program (NY HELPS). For the duration of the NY HELPS Program, this title may be filled via a non-competitive\n                     appointment, which means no examination is required but all candidates must meet the\n                     minimum qualifications of the title for which they apply. Beginning June 26, 2024, all appointments made under this program will be handled\n                     as permanent, non-competitive positions and the official probationary period will\n                     begin on the appointment date. At a future date (within one year of permanent appointment), it is expected employees\n                     hired under NY HELPS will have their non-competitive employment status converted to\n                     competitive status, without having to compete in an examination. Employees will then\n                     be afforded with all of the same rights and privileges of competitive class employees\n                     of New York State. While serving permanently in a NY HELPS title, employees may take\n                     part in any promotion examination for which they are qualified. THERE IS NO EXAM REQUIRED FOR NY HELPS APPOINTMENTS Non-Competitive This class includes those positions for which the State Civil Service Commission has\n               determined that it is not practical to hold a competitive (civil service) examination. \n               However, all must meet minimum qualifications. Positions in this group include \"journeymen\"\n               level positions on the maintenance support staff such as carpenter, electrician or\n               mechanic. Appointment to higher salaried vacant positions are made on the basis of\n               seniority. University employees are given first consideration for CSEA-OSU non-competitive\n               vacancies. This Table Contains a List of Non-Competitive Classified Service Vacancies Grade Title Department Starting Salary Status Posting End Date SG-12 Service & Repair Mechanic (Motor Equipment) Facilities Management $52,694.00 Contingent Permanent, Full-Time 09/03/2026 SG-14 Maintenance Supervisor 1 Facilities Management $59,049.00 Contingent Permanent, Full-Time 09/03/2026 SG-15 Administrative Assistant 2 Division of Advancement $62,477.00 Contingent Permanent, Full-Time 09/13/2026 SG-12 Trades Specialist (Carpenter) Facilities Management $52,694.00 Contingent Permanent, Full-Time 09/14/2026 SG-9 Maintenance Assistant (2nd Shift) Facilities Management $44,560.00 Contingent Permanent, Full-Time 09/14/2026 SG-9 Maintenance Assistant Carpenter Facilities Management $44,560.00 Contingent Permanent, Full-Time 09/14/2026 This Table Contains a List of Non-Competitive, Internal Classified Service Vacancies Grade Title Department Starting Salary Status Posting End Date Labor Class Labor class positions have no minimum educational or experience requirements. University\n               employees are given first consideration for these positions. This table contains a list of Labor Class Classified Service vacancies Labor Class Vacancies Grade Title Department Starting Salary Status Posting End Date SG-6 Facility Operations Assistant 1 - Electrical Facilities Management $37,862.00 Contingent Permanent, Full-Time 09/12/2026 SG-6 Facility Operations Assistant 1 - Carpentry Facilities Management $37,862.00 Contingent Permanent, Full-Time 09/12/2026 SG-6 Facility Operations Assistant 1 (Grounds) Facilities Management $37,862.00 Contingent Permanent, Full-Time 09/12/2026 SG-6 Facility Operations Assistant 1 - Painting Facilities Management $37,862.00 Contingent Permanent, Full-Time 09/12/2026 SG-6 Facility Operations Assistant 1 Facilities Management $37,862.00 Contingent Permanent, Full-Time 09/12/2026 Civil Service Examinations Most New York State civil service examinations are held periodically, such as once\n               a year. Some examinations are held on a continuous recruitment basis. This means that\n               applications are accepted continuously; qualified, applicants are tested on an as-needed\n               basis and successful candidates' names are added to the eligible list continuously. Employment Opportunities with New York State Government Exam Announcements Promotional Exam Announcements Tentative Exam Schedules and more Civil Service WEbsite Clery Act Notification As required by the Clery Act, a copy of Binghamton University's Annual Security Report\n               is available by accessing the following web site: http://asr.binghamton.edu/. You\n               may also obtain a copy of this report by contacting the Office of Human Resources\n               at (607) 777-2187. This report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning\n               reported crimes that occurred on-campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property\n               owned or controlled by Binghamton University; and on public property within, or immediately\n               adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. The report also includes institutional\n               policies concerning campus security, such as policies concerning sexual assault, and\n               other matters. Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer It is the policy of Binghamton University to provide for and promote equal opportunity\n               employment, compensation, and other terms and conditions of employment without discrimination\n               on the basis of age, race, color, religion, disability, national origin, gender identity\n               or expression, sexual orientation, veteran or military service member status, marital\n               status, domestic violence victim status, genetic predisposition or carrier status,\n               or arrest and/or criminal conviction record unless based upon a bona fide occupational\n               qualification or other exception. As required by Title IX and its implementing regulations Binghamton University does\n               not discriminate on the basis of sex in the educational programs and activities which\n               it operates. This requirement extends to employment and admission. Inquiries about\n               sex discrimination may be directed to the University Title IX Coordinator or directly\n               to the Office of Civil Rights (OCR). Contact information for the Title IX Coordinator\n               and OCR, as well as the University's complete Non-Discrimination Notice may be found here . Binghamton University is a tobacco-free campus. Human Resources Jobs Faculty, Librarian and Professional Classified Employment Other Employment Job Fair Prospective Employees Employees Benefits Payroll Retirees Contact Return to Top © 2026 Binghamton University State University of New York Accessibility Emergencies Privacy contact visit share Last Updated: 9/4/26"
    },
    "https://www.binghamton.edu/offices/human-resources/jobs/other.html": {
      "title": "Human Resources: Other Jobs",
      "description": "Human Resources: Other Jobs | Human Resources | Binghamton University Skip to main content Binghamton University: The State University of New York Human Resources search menu Search Human Resources Human Resources Jobs Faculty, Librarian and Professional Classified Employment Other Employment Job Fair Prospective Employees Employees Benefits Payroll Retirees Contact Human Resources: Other Jobs Additional Employment Opportunities Other Employers at Binghamton University Research Foundation The Research Foundation is a private not-for-profit corporation that administers\n                  externally funded sponsored projects for and on behalf of SUNY. The Research Foundation\n                  is a separate employer and offers its own compensation and benefit plans. Chartwells Dining Services Chartwells provides dining services to resident dining halls as well as catering\n                  services at locations across the campus. Barnes and Noble Barnes and Noble operates the campus bookstore. Student Association Jobs include student-run bus company and volunteer ambulance service. Campus Preschool & Early Childhood Center Provides early childhood education to the children of students, faculty and staff\n                  at Binghamton University and the surrounding community. Other Employment Resources New York State Department of Civil Service Vacancies at New York state agencies state-wide. SUNY Employment Vacancies at all State University of New York campuses. Related Information Greater Binghamton Chamber of Commerce Campus Map Human Resources Jobs Faculty, Librarian and Professional Classified Employment Other Employment Job Fair Prospective Employees Employees Benefits Payroll Retirees Contact Return to Top © 2026 Binghamton University State University of New York Accessibility Emergencies Privacy contact visit share Last Updated: 6/8/26"
    },
    "https://www.binghamton.edu/offices/human-resources/jobs/job-fair.html": {
      "title": "Job Fair",
      "description": "Job Fair | Human Resources | Binghamton University Skip to main content Binghamton University: The State University of New York Human Resources search menu Search Human Resources Human Resources Jobs Faculty, Librarian and Professional Classified Employment Other Employment Job Fair Prospective Employees Employees Benefits Payroll Retirees Contact Job Fair BINGHAMTON, N.Y. – Binghamton University will host a job fair from 10 a.m. - 1 p.m. Wednesday, June 24, at the University Union, on campus. A variety of custodial, grounds, maintenance (trades & HVAC), and clerical jobs are\n                  available. University representatives will be on hand to discuss these positions. Attendees should bring résumés or applications the day of the event. On-site job interviews\n                  will take place during the job fair for custodial and maintenance openings. Binghamton University has launched a pilot Employee Referral Bonus program . Applicants must note the employee who referred them at the time of application to\n                  qualify for a $500 payment to both the applicant and current employee. Parking is available in Lot B. Custodial positions are available for the following shifts: Full-time 4 a.m. – 12:30 p.m. 7 a.m. - 3:30 p.m. 5 p.m. – 1 a.m. 11 p.m. – 7 a.m. Weekday and weekend shifts available Half-time (with full benefits) 10 a.m. – 2:30 p.m. (+/- 30 minutes) 4 – 8 a.m. 8 a.m. - 12:00 p.m. 7 a.m. – 3:30 p.m. (Sat., Sun.) 7–11 a.m. (Mon.) Working at Binghamton University As a New York state employer, Binghamton University offers employees a competitive and comprehensive set of benefits . General benefits for faculty and staff include: health insurance/prescription coverage dental and vision insurances Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Flexible Spending Account (FSA) - healthcare, dependent care and adoption advantage care for eligible bargaining units retirement plans and tax-deferred programs access to retirement planning consultations and seminars vacation, holiday, and sick leave accruals Employee tuition assistance Free bus service with ID card Many opportunities for career advancement Full list of positions available at Binghamton University For more information, email Sara DeClemente-Hammoud, director of human resources,\n                  at declemen@binghamton.edu . Human Resources Jobs Faculty, Librarian and Professional Classified Employment Other Employment Job Fair Prospective Employees Employees Benefits Payroll Retirees Contact Return to Top © 2026 Binghamton University State University of New York Accessibility Emergencies Privacy contact visit share Last Updated: 6/2/26"
    },
