    "https://www.binghamton.edu/ccpd/": {
      "title": "Fleishman Career Center",
      "description": "Fleishman Career Center | Binghamton University Skip to main content Binghamton University: The State University of New York Fleishman Career Center search menu Search Fleishman Career Center Fleishman Career Center About Us Student Services and Resources Campus Community For Employers Fleishman Career Center Explore, Pursue, Achieve Career Success hireBing Virtual Career Center Student Career Outcomes Student Employment The Fleishman Impact Removing Barriers for Students’ Career Success $198,731 distributed in grants and funding during 2022–23 105,909 job and internship postings in hireBING by Handshake during 2022–23 200+ employers actively recruit on campus 73% of students engage with career services before junior year Affinity Communities Professional Development Fund Internship Funding What's happening at the Fleishman Career Center Sep 8 Tue Drop-Ins with Peer Industry Mentor Natalie: Tech & Engineering Career Applications 11:00am Sep 8 Tue Excel for Every Career: A Workshop for Pre-Law & Data Analytics Students 7:00pm Sep 9 Wed Fall 2026 In Person Job and Internship Fair (open to all majors) 1:00pm Sep 9 Wed Workforce Recruitment Program Application 101 3:00pm More Events Spring 2026 hours: We are open Monday-Friday, 9:00 a.m. - 4:00 p.m. Schedule a career consulting appointment to discuss any of the following topics: Resumes Job and internship search Career exploration Networking And more! SCHEDULE AN APPOINTMENT Student Testimonials Isabella Kovacs '25 Bella Kovacs discusses how Fleishman Center staff helped her to discover her career\n                              path and gain volunteer and internship experience. Jackson Krajnak '24 Jackson Krajnak reflects on how the Fleishman Center helped him to pick his major,\n                              begin growing his network and create an action plan for his junior year. Kimberly Casey '25 Kimberly Casey used the Fleishman Center to discover her passion for healthcare and\n                              connect with alumni in the industry. Contact information UU-133 careers@binghamton.edu 607-777-2400 Social Media Instagram: @bingfleishmancareer Facebook: facebook.com/Binghamton.Careers/ LinkedIn: linkedin.com/company/fleishman-career Fleishman Career Center About Us Student Services and Resources Campus Community For Employers Return to Top © 2026 Binghamton University State University of New York Accessibility Emergencies Privacy contact visit share Last Updated: 4/6/26"
    },
    "https://binghamton.joinhandshake.com/login": {
      "title": "Get connected",
      "description": "Sign In | Handshake Select language English (US) English (UK) Deutsch Français Select language EN-US EN-UK DE FR Sign up Log in No account? Sign up here. Get connected Binghamton University Login Continue with email Get connected Enter your Binghamton University email Next"
    },
    "https://www.binghamton.edu/offices/human-resources/prospective/dual-career/": {
      "title": "Dual Career Program",
      "description": "Dual Career Program | Human Resources | Binghamton University Skip to main content Binghamton University: The State University of New York Human Resources search menu Search Human Resources Human Resources Jobs Prospective Employees Diversity Living Premier University Dual Career Program DCP Enrollment Form Employees Benefits Payroll Retirees Contact Dual Career Program Binghamton University recognizes the importance of recruiting and retaining outstanding\n               faculty and staff. To assist those who have recently accepted a full-time position\n               at Binghamton, the University offers job-search information to spouses/ partners also\n               seeking employment. Through our Dual Career Program , we can assist your spouse/partner with the job search in a number of ways, including\n               career coaching, résumé development and networking. We also can help obtain non-employment-related\n               information about our community and the area. Eligibility Your spouse/partner is eligible for services through our Dual Career Program if: you have recently received a full-time offer of employment at Binghamton University\n               and you are considering relocating to the Binghamton area, or you have been employed full-time by the University within the past two years and you\n               have relocated to the Binghamton area Services Job-search assistance Information about job openings at Binghamton University Identification as a dual-career candidate for Binghamton University positions Coaching about résumés, cover letters, and interviewing techniques Networking assistance Access to higher-education job information through the Upstate New York Higher Education\n                  Recruitment Consortium website To get started, your spouse/partner should schedule a meeting with our Dual Career\n               Program staff to discuss employment goals, needs and interests. Upon request, they\n               will review your spouses'/partner's résumé or curriculum vitae and other job-search\n               documents and provide appropriate feedback. The Dual Career Program is happy to help your spouse/partner navigate the process,\n               as they play an active, ongoing role in their own job search. Enrollment Form Please complete the enrollment form using the link above to participate in our Dual\n               Career Program. Frequently Asked Questions Q: Am I guaranteed a job? A: There is no guarantee of job placement. We cannot create jobs and we cannot intervene\n               in an employer's hiring process. We will, however, do our best to assist you in your\n               job search. Q: Will I be given preferential treatment for a Binghamton University position? A: Binghamton University is committed to assisting couples facing the challenge of\n               dual careers. You will be able to identify yourself as a dual-career candidate when\n               you apply for Binghamton University positions. Q: Can you help me find employment outside Binghamton University? A: If you're interested in employment elsewhere in the area, we can meet with you\n               to discuss your employment goals and interests and review your application materials. Q: Can you help me find a position at a nearby college or university? A: Binghamton University is a member of the Upstate New York Higher Education Recruitment\n               Consortium. The UNY HERC website (www.unyherc.org) can help you identify jobs available\n               at nearby colleges and universities. The site provides additional information about\n               relocating to the area. Q: How long will you assist me in my job search? A: Program services can continue up to one year. Helpful Links Employment Opportunities at Binghamton University Division of Diversity, Equity and Inclusion Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) The State University of New York and Binghamton University are Equal Opportunity/Affirmative\n               Action Employers. Human Resources Jobs Prospective Employees Diversity Living Premier University Dual Career Program DCP Enrollment Form Employees Benefits Payroll Retirees Contact Return to Top © 2026 Binghamton University State University of New York Accessibility Emergencies Privacy contact visit share Last Updated: 7/31/26"
    },
